<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<office:document xmlns:office="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:office:1.0" xmlns:style="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:style:1.0" xmlns:text="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:text:1.0" xmlns:fo="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:xsl-fo-compatible:1.0" office:mimetype="application/vnd.oasis.opendocument.text" office:version="1.4">
  <office:styles>
    <style:default-style style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:margin-top="0pt" fo:margin-bottom="0pt" fo:line-height="125%"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-family="Arial" fo:font-size="11pt" fo:color="#252722"/>
    </style:default-style>
    <style:style style:name="Title" style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:margin-bottom="16pt"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-size="28pt"/>
    </style:style>
    <style:style style:name="Intro" style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:margin-bottom="10pt"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-size="11pt"/>
    </style:style>
    <style:style style:name="Section" style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:margin-top="10pt" fo:margin-bottom="8pt"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-size="15pt" fo:color="#915039"/>
    </style:style>
    <style:style style:name="Body" style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:margin-bottom="7pt"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-size="11pt"/>
    </style:style>
    <style:style style:name="Bullet" style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:margin-left="18pt" fo:text-indent="0pt" fo:margin-bottom="6pt"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-size="11pt"/>
    </style:style>
    <style:style style:name="Caution" style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:margin-top="7pt"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-size="11pt"/>
    </style:style>
    <style:style style:name="ProjectHeading" style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:break-before="page" fo:margin-bottom="22pt"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-size="15pt" fo:color="#915039"/>
    </style:style>
    <style:style style:name="FieldHeading" style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:margin-top="20pt" fo:margin-bottom="7pt"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-size="12.5pt" fo:font-weight="bold"/>
    </style:style>
    <style:style style:name="FieldNote" style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:margin-bottom="7pt"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-size="11pt"/>
    </style:style>
    <style:style style:name="FooterFirst" style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:margin-top="300pt"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-size="10pt"/>
    </style:style>
    <style:style style:name="FooterSecond" style:family="paragraph">
      <style:paragraph-properties fo:margin-top="76pt"/>
      <style:text-properties fo:font-size="10pt"/>
    </style:style>
  </office:styles>
  <office:automatic-styles>
    <style:page-layout style:name="PageLayout">
      <style:page-layout-properties fo:page-width="8.5in" fo:page-height="11in" fo:margin-left="0.7in" fo:margin-right="0.7in" fo:margin-top="0.55in" fo:margin-bottom="0.45in"/>
    </style:page-layout>
  </office:automatic-styles>
  <office:master-styles>
    <style:master-page style:name="Standard" style:page-layout-name="PageLayout"/>
  </office:master-styles>
  <office:body>
    <office:text>
      <text:p text:style-name="Title">Interior design proposal template</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Intro">Blank editable template</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Intro">OpenLintel • Educational planning resource • September 26, 2026</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Illustrative teaching extension of The Window Room; not a client record, supplier quote, site survey, or construction-ready document. Pending professional review.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Section">How to use</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Adapt the outline to the services you actually offer. The example is a fictional teaching document with no quoted fee, real client, or enforceable terms. It is not a contract and does not replace professional legal review of an agreement. Check every proposed output against your actual services; separate unpriced items, allowances, and exclusions.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Summarize discovery in the client’s language.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Pair each proposed deliverable with a clear phase and review.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Discuss assumptions and exclusions before preparing a separate agreement.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Section">Review before use</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Do not copy sample services into an offer you cannot deliver.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Do not mix design fees with the furniture purchasing budget.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Do not present this educational proposal outline as a legal contract.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Caution">Replace illustrative information with verified project records. No approval, legal agreement, or construction readiness is represented. Keep completed client documents in your own secure system.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FooterFirst">OpenLintel • Planning resource • 1</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="ProjectHeading">Your project</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Project understanding</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">Restate the client’s intended outcome and identify the information you have relied on.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Proposed approach</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">Explain the sequence and where client decisions will be needed.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Proposed deliverables</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">Name each output and the level of development. Avoid an undefined promise of “all drawings”.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Phases and reviews</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">Describe review gates rather than inventing a universal project duration.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Fee discussion</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">List the services to be priced and the basis for discussion. Keep purchasing allowances separate from professional fees.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Assumptions and exclusions</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">Identify missing inputs, specialist work, procurement responsibilities, and what this proposal does not include.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldHeading">Next steps</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">Name the information needed to develop an agreement. Do not use this outline as a substitute for legal terms.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FieldNote">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FooterSecond">OpenLintel • Planning resource • 2</text:p>
    </office:text>
  </office:body>
</office:document>